family: softflowd
what: flow
transport: v9
address: 192.0.2.10
verification: tested
reference: softflowd(8) manual page (-i, -n, -v, -t)
does: Runs softflowd on <INTERFACE> and exports the flows it sees to Woodshed as flow v9 (RFC 3954).
check: Woodshed's Flows view lists this machine as an exporter within a minute or two; `softflowctl statistics` shows the flows it has sent.
placeholders: <INTERFACE>
addresses: 192.0.2.10 2001:db8::10 logs-01.example.net logs-01
notes:
- Woodshed's flow listener is off: turn it on in Settings → Flows (or `woodshed flow on`, as an administrator) first.
- <INTERFACE> is the network interface to watch, as `ip link` names it.
- -t maxlife=60 exports long-running flows every minute, so they show up during an incident rather than when they end.
- softflowd sees only the traffic that passes the interface it watches.
---- part command "": Run softflowd (as root), or put the same options in your distribution's softflowd service settings
softflowd -i <INTERFACE> -n 192.0.2.10:2055 -v 9 -t maxlife=60
---- part command "": See what it's exporting
softflowctl statistics
==== text
# Run softflowd (as root), or put the same options in your distribution's softflowd service settings
softflowd -i <INTERFACE> -n 192.0.2.10:2055 -v 9 -t maxlife=60

# See what it's exporting
softflowctl statistics
